policy-capability-transient-handle: a transient handle exists only if it is loaded

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Part 3, version 185, TPM2_PolicyCapability): "If the
requested TPM *property* does not exist, the TPM will return `TPM_RC_POLICY`
unless the *operation* is `TPM_EO_NEQ`", with the property type `TPM_HANDLE`
for `TPM_CAP_HANDLES`.

ObjectCapGetOneLoaded() loops over every object slot from the handle's slot
on and returns TRUE for the first occupied one, so TPM2_PolicyCapability
(TPM_CAP_HANDLES) reports a transient handle as existing (and compares the
handle value itself) whenever any object with a larger handle is loaded. The
patch checks only the handle's own slot.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Object.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Object.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Object.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/subsystem/Object.c
@@ -868,20 +868,19 @@ ObjectCapGetLoaded(TPMI_DH_OBJECT handle,     // IN: start handle
 // This function returns whether a handle is loaded.
 BOOL ObjectCapGetOneLoaded(TPMI_DH_OBJECT handle)  // IN: handle
 {
-    UINT32 i;
+    UINT32 i = handle - TRANSIENT_FIRST;
 
     pAssert_BOOL(HandleGetType(handle) == TPM_HT_TRANSIENT);
 
-    // Iterate object slots to get loaded object handles
-    for(i = handle - TRANSIENT_FIRST; i < MAX_LOADED_OBJECTS; i++)
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the handle exists only if an object is loaded in exactly its slot (the
+    // original loop reported any loaded object at or after the handle's slot).
+    if(i < MAX_LOADED_OBJECTS && s_objects[i].attributes.occupied == TRUE)
     {
-        if(s_objects[i].attributes.occupied == TRUE)
-        {
-            // A valid transient object can not be the copy of a persistent object
-            pAssert_BOOL(s_objects[i].attributes.evict == CLEAR);
+        // A valid transient object can not be the copy of a persistent object
+        pAssert_BOOL(s_objects[i].attributes.evict == CLEAR);
 
-            return TRUE;
-        }
+        return TRUE;
     }
 
     return FALSE;
